  "question": {
    "text": "The ratio of speed of sound in hydrogen gas to the speed of sound in oxygen gas at the same temperature is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>4</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The formula to calculate the speed of sound in hydrogen gas is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mfrac></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>The formula to calculate the speed of sound in oxygen is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi><mi>R</mi><mi>T</mi></mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mfrac></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Divide equation (1) by (2) and simplify to obtain the required ratio.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>v</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><msub><mi>M</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi>M</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mfrac></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Substitute the values of the known parameters into equation (3) to calculate the required ratio.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mfrac><msub><mi>v</mi><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><msub><mi>O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mfrac></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><msqrt><mfrac><mn>32</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msqrt></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p></blockquote>"
